-- title:
--   Switcheroo Self Consistency Bip
-- statement:
--   **One-question switcheroo self consistency converts to the bipartite relation used by transfer lemmas.**
--
--   Let `M` satisfy the switcheroo `SDDRel` at error `omega` over the uniform slice-question distribution. Regard the indexed projective submeasurement as an ordinary indexed submeasurement on both sides. Then the corresponding bipartite `BipartiteSDDRel` holds with the same state, distribution, families, and error:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}(\psi_{bi},\mathcal D_{\mathrm{slice}},M_{\mathrm{left}},M_{\mathrm{right}},\omega)
--   \Longrightarrow
--   \operatorname{BipartiteSDDRel}(\psi_{bi},\mathcal D_{\mathrm{slice}},M,M,\omega).
--   $$
--
--   This is a representation change rather than a loss in the error parameter. It supplies the form expected by the left- and right-transfer estimates in the first and second aggregate-term bounds.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooSelfConsistency_bip`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
